Defense in Depth","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth","02.platform\u002F06.defense-in-depth",{"title":176,"path":177,"stem":178,"icon":179},"MCP Tools","\u002Fplatform\u002Fmcp-tools","02.platform\u002F07.mcp-tools","i-lucide-bot",{"title":181,"path":182,"stem":183,"icon":184},"Observability","\u002Fplatform\u002Fobservability","02.platform\u002F08.observability","i-lucide-activity",{"title":186,"path":187,"stem":188,"icon":189},"Contributing","\u002Fplatform\u002Fcontributing","02.platform\u002F09.contributing","i-lucide-git-pull-request",{"title":191,"path":192,"stem":193,"icon":194},"System Migrations","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsystem-migrations","02.platform\u002F10.system-migrations","i-lucide-database-zap",{"title":196,"path":197,"stem":198,"icon":199},"Service Call Liveness","\u002Fplatform\u002Fservice-call-liveness","02.platform\u002F11.service-call-liveness","i-lucide-heart-pulse",{"title":128,"icon":129,"path":201,"stem":202,"children":203,"page":36},"\u002Fplatform\u002Freference","02.platform\u002F12.reference",[204,209,214],{"title":205,"path":206,"stem":207,"icon":208},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":210,"path":211,"stem":212,"icon":213},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":215,"path":216,"stem":217,"icon":151},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":219,"path":220,"stem":221,"icon":222},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","02.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":224,"path":225,"stem":226,"icon":227},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","02.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"id":229,"title":33,"body":230,"description":517,"extension":518,"links":519,"meta":520,"navigation":521,"path":34,"seo":522,"stem":35,"__hash__":523},"docs\u002F01.apps\u002F03.application-structure\u002F03.artifact-types.md",{"type":231,"value":232,"toc":507},"minimark",[233,242,246,249,254,278,283,294,297,301,308,312,320,324,339,342,346,349,353,361,365,373,377,380,384,389,393,398,402,405,409,414,418,426,430,433,504],[234,235,236,237,241],"p",{},"Every project in a Kinotic application contributes one or more ",[238,239,240],"strong",{},"artifacts",". An artifact is a typed output that the platform knows how to build, deploy, and manage. This page describes each artifact type and when to use it.",[243,244,59],"h2",{"id":245},"persistence",[234,247,248],{},"The most common starting point. A persistence artifact defines your domain models (entities) and gets auto-generated CRUD services in return.",[234,250,251],{},[238,252,253],{},"What you provide:",[255,256,257],"ul",{},[258,259,260,261,265,266,269,270,273,274,277],"li",{},"Entity classes decorated with ",[262,263,264],"code",{},"@Entity"," and field-level annotations like ",[262,267,268],{},"@NotNull",", ",[262,271,272],{},"@Precision",", and ",[262,275,276],{},"@AutoGeneratedId",".",[234,279,280],{},[238,281,282],{},"What the platform provides:",[255,284,285,288,291],{},[258,286,287],{},"Full CRUD operations (save, find, delete) with pagination and sorting.",[258,289,290],{},"Named queries derived from method naming conventions.",[258,292,293],{},"Automatic storage provisioning and indexing.",[234,295,296],{},"Persistence is typically the first artifact you create because it establishes the data model that the rest of the application builds on.",[243,298,300],{"id":299},"microservice","Microservice",[234,302,303,304,277],{},"A microservice artifact is long-running code that executes in a pod or VM. It publishes services that other parts of the application can discover and call through ",[305,306,307],"a",{"href":52},"service proxies",[234,309,310],{},[238,311,253],{},[255,313,314,317],{},[258,315,316],{},"TypeScript classes that implement your business logic.",[258,318,319],{},"Service interfaces that you want to expose to the rest of the application.",[234,321,322],{},[238,323,282],{},[255,325,326,329,336],{},[258,327,328],{},"Automatic service registration in the Service Directory.",[258,330,331,332,335],{},"Service discovery and zone-based routing so other projects can call your service through a ",[305,333,334],{"href":52},"service proxy"," with a simple function call.",[258,337,338],{},"Lifecycle management, scaling, and health monitoring.",[234,340,341],{},"Use a microservice when your logic goes beyond simple CRUD -- orchestrating across multiple entities, calling external APIs, or running long-lived workflows.",[243,343,345],{"id":344},"batch-job","Batch Job",[234,347,348],{},"A batch job artifact is code that runs on a schedule. It is ideal for periodic tasks like data aggregation, report generation, cleanup routines, or syncing with external systems.",[234,350,351],{},[238,352,253],{},[255,354,355,358],{},[258,356,357],{},"TypeScript code that performs the job.",[258,359,360],{},"A schedule definition (cron expression or interval).",[234,362,363],{},[238,364,282],{},[255,366,367,370],{},[258,368,369],{},"Scheduled execution with retry and failure handling.",[258,371,372],{},"Logging and observability for each run.",[243,374,376],{"id":375},"ui-component","UI Component",[234,378,379],{},"A UI component artifact produces reusable building blocks that can be shared across multiple frontends within the application. Think of it as an internal component library.",[234,381,382],{},[238,383,253],{},[255,385,386],{},[258,387,388],{},"Reusable UI components packaged for consumption by frontend projects.",[234,390,391],{},[238,392,282],{},[255,394,395],{},[258,396,397],{},"Versioning and distribution within the application.",[243,399,401],{"id":400},"frontend","Frontend",[234,403,404],{},"A frontend artifact is a complete user interface that gets deployed as a static site. It consumes services published by other projects in the application.",[234,406,407],{},[238,408,253],{},[255,410,411],{},[258,412,413],{},"A web application (built with any framework) that compiles to static assets.",[234,415,416],{},[238,417,282],{},[255,419,420,423],{},[258,421,422],{},"Static hosting with CDN distribution.",[258,424,425],{},"Automatic connection to the application's services through the Kinotic client libraries.",[243,427,429],{"id":428},"combining-artifact-types","Combining Artifact Types",[234,431,432],{},"Most real-world applications combine several artifact types. A typical setup might look like this:",[434,435,436,452],"table",{},[437,438,439],"thead",{},[440,441,442,446,449],"tr",{},[443,444,445],"th",{},"Project",[443,447,448],{},"Artifact Type",[443,450,451],{},"Role",[453,454,455,468,480,492],"tbody",{},[440,456,457,463,465],{},[458,459,460],"td",{},[262,461,462],{},"data",[458,464,59],{},[458,466,467],{},"Defines entities and provides auto-generated CRUD services",[440,469,470,475,477],{},[458,471,472],{},[262,473,474],{},"services",[458,476,300],{},[458,478,479],{},"Implements business rules that orchestrate across entities",[440,481,482,487,489],{},[458,483,484],{},[262,485,486],{},"jobs",[458,488,345],{},[458,490,491],{},"Runs nightly data aggregation",[440,493,494,499,501],{},[458,495,496],{},[262,497,498],{},"web",[458,500,401],{},[458,502,503],{},"The main user interface",[234,505,506],{},"Each project is independently developed and versioned, but they all deploy as part of the same application and communicate through the Service Directory.",{"title":508,"searchDepth":509,"depth":509,"links":510},"",2,[511,512,513,514,515,516],{"id":245,"depth":509,"text":59},{"id":299,"depth":509,"text":300},{"id":344,"depth":509,"text":345},{"id":375,"depth":509,"text":376},{"id":400,"depth":509,"text":401},{"id":428,"depth":509,"text":429},"Learn about the different artifact types a Kinotic project can contribute -- from persistence and microservices to frontends.","md",null,{},true,{"title":33,"description":517},"ks4mH_HWM4uaDA9Vwx-yIdl366mKkKWDw9PgfC_UDoU",[525,527],{"title":29,"path":30,"stem":31,"description":526,"children":-1},"Learn how to configure Kinotic applications and the projects that compose them.",{"title":25,"path":44,"stem":45,"description":528,"children":-1},"How services work in Kinotic and the communication patterns they support.",1790405985515]